Slot 017 is spent, not free.

No migration was ever written here. The author of
018_prune_prefix_duplicate_indexes.sql numbered from 018 while the highest
slot in use was 016, so 017 was skipped rather than deleted -- there is no
017 in this directory's history and no database has a tracking row for it.

The slot is tombstoned rather than filled, because 018 and 019 are already
pushed and a migration that has shipped cannot be renumbered: the runner
keys a tracking row on the version and refuses the checksum change, so a
deployment that applied 018 would reject its replacement at the next boot.

Numbering continues at the highest slot ever used, never at the first gap.
